  "description": "Reusable .NET 10 package that wraps ASP.NET Core Identity with cookie and JWT auth, Google OAuth, a pluggable e-mail provider, a multi-tenant model with dynamic RBAC (roles + module permissions), and secure defaults — wired up with a single AddMyIdentity call. JWT and Google OAuth secrets are supplied by the consumer (never shipped in the package).",
  "id": "MyIdentity",
  "isPrerelease": true,
  "lastEdited": "2026-07-31T03:08:05.39Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "XNkhYjoRpOwXzh4pr4LaZPs/keuNzOh61zaqeyrvBR2sJtUd8tUblfD/DpxMuib5ao7ZSlZ001RIZjj8EK1jMQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 223835,
  "published": "2026-07-31T03:05:25.467Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v4.0.0-alpha.11: two items from a consumer smoke test, neither breaking. Added GetMyUserRoleAssignmentsAsync() on IMyIdentityPermissionAdminService: reading your OWN role assignments is not an administrative operation, but GetUserRoleAssignmentsAsync (admin-gated by design, since enumerating the tenant-wide who-has-which-role map is sensitive) was the only read available, so a profile page listing the signed-in user roles failed for every plain member with \"Only administrators can manage role assignments\". The subject is resolved from the authenticated principal and never from caller input; the Tier-3 gate on the wide read is unchanged and now pinned by a test. Fixed: ProcessGoogleResponseAsync had nine refusal paths, eight logging Warning unconditionally and one -- no local user and RegisterIfNotExist false, the most common cause of a failed Google sign-in -- logging at Debug behind DebugLogEnabled, so the most frequent failure produced no log line at all; it now logs Warning like its siblings. BlazorExample Mi Perfil demonstrates the new self-service read. See UPGRADE.md 24. API may still change before stable.",
